{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790015024,"nonce":"lXc/QaBUdsTgw3LUF+9jS5W0r0Y=","title":"No verb loads a save: testing save/load means swapping autostart.rws and relaunching","message":"Found while testing Prison Standards on the bench, 2026-09-21.\n\n## The gap\n`save` exists, but nothing loads a save.\n\nTesting save/load mid-job therefore meant: `save` → stop the game → copy the save over `Saves/autostart.rws` → relaunch without `--quicktest` → put the original autostart back afterwards. The saves in question:\n- a capture partway through its strip toil;\n- a save file edited to mark beds for prisoners (see 9717e52).\n\nThat is slow, it touches the parked `autostart.rws` (the playbook's quicktest-and-autostart-collide lesson), and it is one more thing to restore.\n\n## Ask\n`load {name}`: load a save from the bench's Saves folder the way the game's Load menu does. The result returns once the game is playable again, with the new sid and tick. The journal marks the load, so the watermark and the \"no earlier screen\" logic (975973e) stay right.\n\n## Acceptance\n- `load {name: \"x\"}` on a running bench returns `ok` with the loaded tick. After that, `status` is `ok` and every verb works on the loaded game.\n- An unknown name is refused before anything is unloaded.\n- The journal shows a load event between the two sessions' entries.","files":null}]}